---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Homelab Infrastructure | Architecture">
    <h1>/etc/infrastructure/homelab.conf</h1>
    <blockquote>
        I live and breathe infrastructure. Outside of enterprise environments, I test boundaries, simulate edge-case network topologies, and experiment with bare-metal configurations inside a dedicated home deployment.
    </blockquote>
    <hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #334155; margin: 2em 0;" />
    <h2>Core Hardware Blueprint</h2>
    <h3>1. Rack Enclosure & Base Systems</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Cabinet Tier:</strong> 42RU Industrial Enclosure (Fully structured patch configurations, custom power paths).</li>
        <li><strong>Compute Footprint:</strong> HP ProLiant, Dell, and Cisco UCS high-density rack gear.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>2. Bare-Metal Containers & Orchestration</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Cluster Pools:</strong> Cohesive 4-Node hybrid bare-metal cluster running production-tier orchestrations.</li>
        <li><strong>Runtime Architectures:</strong> Dual setups exploring multi-tenant Kubernetes and Docker Swarm deployments to benchmark deployment speed and state persistence models under synthetic failures.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>3. Compute-Intensive AI Cluster</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>GPU Topology:</strong> Fully dedicated 4x GPU hardware platform customized for machine learning and artificial intelligence workflows.</li>
        <li><strong>Models Hosted:</strong> Active local endpoints for PyTorch and Transformers pipelines, localized Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) frameworks, and optimized deepseek/Llama architectures.</li>
    </ul>
</Layout>